/**
 * Manrope 400 / 700, the same typeface invoice_pdf.dart uses in the app, so the
 * WhatsApp invoice matches it — and so the rupee sign renders at all (pdf-lib's
 * built-in Helvetica is WinAnsi and throws on U+20B9).
 *
 * Subset to the ranges in SUPPORTED_TEXT below (21 KB each vs 94 KB full), and
 * inlined rather than fetched so a cold start needs no network.
 *
 * Regenerate:
 *   python3 -m fontTools.subset assets/fonts/Manrope_400Regular.ttf \
 *     --unicodes="U+0020-007E,U+00A0-00FF,U+2013,U+2014,U+2018,U+2019,U+201C,U+201D,U+2022,U+2212,U+20B9" \
 *     --layout-features='' --no-hinting --desubroutinize --output-file=out.ttf
 */

/** Exactly the codepoints the subset covers. Anything else is stripped before
 * it reaches pdf-lib, which would otherwise throw mid-send on, say, a gym whose
 * name or address is in Devanagari. */
